<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Tenant API Documentation · OpenWeb PBX</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/app/pbx_api_docs/docs.css?v=1"><script src="/app/pbx_api_docs/docs.js?v=1" defer></script></head>
<body><a class="skip" href="#content">Skip to documentation</a><header><a class="brand" href="/core/desktop/">OpenWeb PBX</a><nav aria-label="Tenant API"><a href="/tenantadmin/">Tenant Admin</a><a href="/app/pbx_api_keys/">API Keys</a><a href="/api-docs?format=openapi">Download OpenAPI</a></nav></header>
<main id="content"><section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">TENANT ADMINISTRATION API · <?=$e($spec['info']['version'])?></p><h1>One tenant. All your CloudPBXs.</h1><p>Manage this tenant’s users, trunks, incoming numbers, call routing, templates, backups and services from your own software. The same permissions apply to the admin dashboard and API.</p><p class="address">API address <code><?=$e($base)?></code></p><a class="button" href="/app/pbx_api_keys/">Create an API key</a> <a class="button secondary" href="#reference">Browse <?=$count?> operations</a></section>
<section id="start"><h2>Start with a full tenant administrator key</h2><ol><li>Sign in as the tenant administrator and open <a href="/app/pbx_api_keys/">API Keys</a>.</li><li>Choose your tenant. Select <strong>Full tenant administration</strong>; PBX service becomes <strong>All services in the selected tenant</strong>.</li><li>Name the integration, choose its expiry and create the key. Save the secret immediately; it is displayed only once.</li><li>Send it in <code>Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY</code>. Call <code>GET /services</code> to find the <code>domain_uuid</code> of the configured CloudPBX you want to manage.</li></ol><aside>A tenant-wide key covers that tenant’s current and future services. To limit it to one CloudPBX, select that PBX instead. A PBX-specific key cannot create tenant services or manage tenant-wide templates. Your platform login workspace is not a calling PBX.</aside>
<pre><code>curl --fail-with-body \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $OPENWEBPBX_API_KEY" \
  "<?=$e($base)?>/services"</code></pre>
<p>Read <code>data[].domain_uuid</code> and use the chosen value in PBX URLs. API results are wrapped in <code>{"data": ..., "request_id": "..."}</code>. Never put the secret in a URL, browser script, Git repository or QR code.</p>
<pre><code>curl --fail-with-body \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $OPENWEBPBX_API_KEY" \
  "<?=$e($base)?>/pbx/YOUR_SERVICE_DOMAIN_UUID/users"</code></pre></section>
<section id="permissions"><h2>What full tenant administration includes</h2><p>The preset selects the following permissions. Each request still requires the owner’s current administrator role, an enabled tenant and an authorised PBX. It cannot manage another tenant, global SMTP, server settings or instance backups. Reseller and instance administration use separately authorised keys. The hostname identifies this installation; changing a hostname, tenant UUID or PBX UUID never grants additional access.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Permission</th><th>Access</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach($scopes as $scope=>$label):?><tr><td><code><?=$e($scope)?></code></td><td><?=$e($label)?></td></tr><?php endforeach;?></tbody></table></div><p>Delegated keys inherit the exact tenant and PBX boundary, may have fewer permissions and cannot outlive their parent. Revoking or rotating a parent withdraws its descendants. Disabled users, removed roles and suspended tenants lose access on the next request.</p></section>
<section id="workflows"><h2>Common workflows</h2><ul><li><strong>Create a CloudPBX:</strong> list <code>/templates</code>, select a published template and use <code>POST /services</code>. Supply your tenant UUID, a service name and a stable <code>request_uuid</code> for retries. Existing resource allowances and managed-domain registration remain enforced.</li><li><strong>Users and phones:</strong> use <code>/pbx/{domain_uuid}/users</code>; the returned <code>data.id</code> is the extension number. To retrieve its existing QR setup, call <code>actions/phone-qr</code> with <code>{"number":"1000"}</code>. Encode the exact private <code>data.payload</code> string. Reading it does not rotate a stable QR.</li><li><strong>Numbers and routing:</strong> use the DID editor and <code>/dids</code> operations so the same routing validation applies as in the dashboard. Routes can target extensions, ring groups, digital receptionists and Call Me Back.</li><li><strong>Backups:</strong> use the tenant backup endpoints. Verify an archive before an explicitly confirmed restore. Accepted jobs must be polled to completion; HTTP200 is not proof that a restore completed.</li><li><strong>Personal accounts:</strong> end users and department staff create separate account keys in My PBX. Their role-scoped reference remains available in the <a href="https://openwebpbx.com/api-docs#administration-v2">complete public API documentation</a>; full tenant keys do not impersonate an end user.</li></ul></section>
<section id="errors"><h2>Errors and limits</h2><p>Use HTTPS from your server. Administration requests with a browser <code>Origin</code> are refused. JSON is limited to128KiB and each key to120 requests per minute. Phone passwords and registration tokens are not API keys.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Response</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>401</td><td>Missing bearer key.</td></tr><tr><td>403</td><td>Key expired, revoked, outside its scope, or its owner no longer has permission.</td></tr><tr><td>409 <code>pbx_not_configured</code></td><td>Select an active CloudPBX from <code>/services</code>, not an empty tenant/platform login workspace. Do not reset or initialise customer data.</td></tr><tr><td>409</td><td>Conflict, resource limit or another operation is running.</td></tr><tr><td>429</td><td>Wait for <code>Retry-After</code> before retrying.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Keep <code>request_id</code> for support. Do not log credentials, QR payloads or private backups. A request UUID makes supported service creation retries idempotent; it does not make every command automatically safe to repeat.</p></section>
<section id="reference"><h2>Tenant API reference</h2><p>Paths below are relative to <code><?=$e($base)?></code>. This reference is generated from the implemented API contract and excludes instance and reseller operations.</p><label class="filter">Find an endpoint<input id="endpoint-filter" type="search" placeholder="Users, trunks, backups, Call Me Back…" autocomplete="off"></label><p id="endpoint-count" role="status" aria-live="polite"><?=$count?> operations</p>
<?php foreach($spec['paths'] as $path=>$methods):foreach($methods as $method=>$op):?><details data-endpoint><summary><span class="method <?=$e($method)?>"><?=$e(strtoupper($method))?></span><code><?=$e($path)?></code><span><?=$e($op['summary'])?></span></summary><div class="endpoint-body"><p><?=$e($op['description'])?></p><?php if(!empty($op['parameters'])):?><h3>Parameters</h3><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Where</th><th>Required</th><th>Rules</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach($op['parameters'] as $parameter):?><tr><td><code><?=$e($parameter['name'])?></code></td><td><?=$e($parameter['in'])?></td><td><?=!empty($parameter['required'])?'Yes':'No'?></td><td><?=$e($json($parameter['schema']??[]))?></td></tr><?php endforeach;?></tbody></table></div><?php endif;?><?php foreach($op['requestBody']['content']??[] as $mime=>$body):?><h3>Request · <?=$e($mime)?></h3><?php $schema=$body['schema']??[];if(isset($schema['$ref']))$schema=$spec['components']['schemas'][basename($schema['$ref'])]??$schema;?><pre><code><?=$e($json($schema))?></code></pre><?php if(isset($body['example'])):?><h3>Example body</h3><pre><code><?=$e($json($body['example']))?></code></pre><?php endif;?><?php endforeach;?><p>Responses: <?=$e(implode(', ',array_keys($op['responses'])))?>. <a href="/api-docs?format=openapi">Download the OpenAPI document</a> for complete referenced schemas and response contracts.</p></div></details><?php endforeach;endforeach;?>
</section><footer><p>OpenWeb PBX · <a href="/app/pbx_api_keys/">API Keys</a> · <a href="https://openwebpbx.com/privacy">Privacy</a> · <a href="https://openwebpbx.com/terms">Terms</a></p></footer></main></body></html>
